From: kotwicha
Subject: [PATCH] Input: synaptics - keep the RMI4 sensor awake on the ThinkPad T14/P14s Gen 1 AMD

On the Synaptics TM3471 in the ThinkPad T14/P14s Gen 1 AMD (LEN2064)
driven over RMI4/SMBus, the doze interval of 6 that Lenovo's Windows
driver programs is not enough: two-finger scrolls are still reported
as pinches. Setting the F01 NoSleep bit removes the misfires.

Restore LEN2064 to smbus_pnp_ids, now that i2c-piix4 provides SMBus
Host Notify through the ASF target block, and add
psmouse.synaptics_rmi_nosleep (-1 = known pads, 0 = never, 1 = always)
so other pads can opt in without a rebuild.
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c b/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c
--- a/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c
+++ b/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c
@@ -191,6 +191,7 @@ static const char * const smbus_pnp_ids[] = {
 	"LEN2054", /* E480 */
 	"LEN2055", /* E580 */
 	"LEN2058", /* E490 */
+	"LEN2064",
 	"LEN2068", /* T14 Gen 1 */
 	"LEN2073",
 	"SYN1221", /* TUXEDO InfinityBook Pro 14 v5 */
@@ -1782,6 +1783,23 @@ static int synaptics_intertouch = IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_RMI4_SMB) ?
 module_param_named(synaptics_intertouch, synaptics_intertouch, int, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(synaptics_intertouch, "Use a secondary bus for the Synaptics device.");
 
+static const char * const rmi_nosleep_pnp_ids[] = {
+	"LEN2064",
+	NULL
+};
+
+static int synaptics_rmi_nosleep = -1;
+module_param_named(synaptics_rmi_nosleep, synaptics_rmi_nosleep, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(synaptics_rmi_nosleep, "Keep the RMI4 sensor awake between touches (-1 = known pads, 0 = never, 1 = always).");
+
+static bool synaptics_rmi_keep_awake(struct psmouse *psmouse)
+{
+	if (synaptics_rmi_nosleep >= 0)
+		return synaptics_rmi_nosleep;
+
+	return psmouse_matches_pnp_id(psmouse, rmi_nosleep_pnp_ids);
+}
+
 static const char * const lenovo_doze_pnp_ids[] = {
 	"LEN040D",
 	"LEN040E",
@@ -1816,6 +1834,8 @@ static int synaptics_create_intertouch(struct psmouse *psmouse,
 		.reset_delay_ms = 30,
 		.power_management = {
 			.doze_interval = synaptics_doze(psmouse),
+			.nosleep = synaptics_rmi_keep_awake(psmouse) ?
+					RMI_REG_STATE_ON : RMI_REG_STATE_DEFAULT,
 		},
 		.sensor_pdata = {
 			.sensor_type = rmi_sensor_touchpad,
